{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the princes brought the shoham stones.</b> Since the way of the prince is to exalt himself over the people, in the manner of what is written concerning a king (Deuteronomy 17): לבלתי רום לבבו מאחיו — 'that his heart not be lifted up above his brethren,' therefore the princes brought stones that would be upon the heart of Aharon, so that they might gain atonement for the haughtiness of their heart. And therefore he marked their donation with the definite article, namely 'the shoham stones' and 'the stones of the filling' — the stones that Israel lacked. And the intention of the princes was that all would donate first for the work of the Mishkan and that they would then complete whatever all Israel lacked. And even though their intention was for the good, it was reckoned to them as a sin and a deficiency, because they were relying on this matter — for perhaps Israel would have brought the stones and their intention would not have been fulfilled, since they would have completed everything and the princes would have no portion in the commandment of the Mishkan. And therefore you find והנשיאים written deficient (without the letter י), as והנשאם. And from here comes a punishment for everyone who is able to be among the first in a commandment but is not first; and because of this their name was written deficient." "<b>And there are those</b> who explained that the shoham stones and the other things came to Israel by way of miracle, and in order that the work of the Mishkan be completed, the clouds of glory brought them into the tent of Mosheh. And this is the sense of והנשיאים הביאו from the root of (Psalms 135:7): מעלה נשיאים מקצה הארץ — 'He brings up clouds from the ends of the earth.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "Rabbeinu Bahya's source citation reads simply (שם י״ז), referring back to an earlier-cited passage; the reference is to Deuteronomy 17:20 (לבלתי רום לבבו מאחיו). The verse phrase quoted matches Deut. 17:20, though the chapter reference was resolved by context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:30.630833341Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}